<article class="doc">
  <h1>Refund Policy</h1>
  <p class="updated">Last updated: November 15, 2026</p>

  <h2>Bought on mailkin.app</h2>
  <p>If Mailkin isn't right for you, you can get a <strong>full refund within 14 days</strong> of your purchase, for any reason.</p>
  <p>To ask for one, email <a href="mailto:macapps.support@icloud.com">macapps.support@icloud.com</a> with the email address you used to buy, or reply to your receipt email. You can also contact Paddle, our reseller and Merchant of Record, through <a href="https://paddle.net">paddle.net</a>. Refunds go back to your original payment method. Your bank may take a few days to show it.</p>
  <p>After a refund, the license key from that purchase is deactivated and Mailkin goes back to the free allowance.</p>
  <p>After 14 days, purchases are generally not refundable, but write to us if something went wrong and we will look at it. This doesn't affect your statutory rights as a consumer.</p>

  <h2>Bought on the Mac App Store</h2>
  <p>Apple handles payments and refunds for App Store purchases. Request a refund at <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.</p>
</article>
